Domain: Orders
  An order is placed and submitted, the outside checks the customer's credit, and the order is approved or declined.

Aggregate: Order
  An order a customer places.

  An order is identified by its number.

  It has:
    a number: order number
    a customer: customer name
    a reason: reason, optional

  An order number has a value: text.
    Rule "an order has a number" holds when the value is not empty

  A customer name has a value: text.
    Rule "an order has a customer" holds when the value is not empty

  A reason has a value: text.

  Lifecycle: status, starting as draft
    Submit moves an order from draft to submitted
    Approve moves an order from submitted to approved
    Decline moves an order from submitted to declined

  Command: Place
    Goal: Start an order
    Who: Customer
    When a number and a customer are given
    Then the number and the customer are set
    And OrderPlaced is announced

  Command: Submit
    Goal: Send a placed order off for its credit check
    Who: Customer
    It acts on an existing order
    Given "only a draft can be submitted" holds when the status is draft
    Then OrderSubmitted is announced

  Command: Approve
    Goal: Accept an order whose credit cleared
    It acts on an existing order
    Given "only a submitted order can be approved" holds when the status is submitted
    Then OrderApproved is announced

  Command: Decline
    Goal: Turn down an order whose credit was refused
    It acts on an existing order
    When a reason is given
    Given "only a submitted order can be declined" holds when the status is submitted
    Then the reason is set
    And OrderDeclined is announced

Policy: Check Credit When Submitted
  Whenever OrderSubmitted is announced
  Then check credit is asked

Policy: Approve When Credit Clears
  Whenever CreditCleared is announced by an order
  Then Approve runs

Policy: Decline When Credit Is Refused
  Whenever CreditRefused is announced by an order
  Then Decline runs with the reason
